(Abstract) Tj T*
/F2 10 Tf
14 TL
(The belief that beekeepers live longer than anyone else is present since ages. However, no ) Tj T*
(research has been done to explore the longevity of life in beekeepers. Here, we investigated ) Tj T*
(the telomere length in 30 male beekeepers and 30 male non-beekeepers and associated them with ) Tj T*
(the longevity of life using Southern analysis of terminal restriction fragments \(TRFs\) ) Tj T*
(generated by Hinf I/Rsa I digestion of human genomic DNA using TeloTAGGG Telomere Length ) Tj T*
(Assay. Interestingly, we found that the telomere length of male beekeepers was significantly ) Tj T*
(longer than those of male non-beekeepers with a p value of less than 0.05, suggesting that ) Tj T*
(beekeepers may have longer life compared to non-beekeepers. We further found that the ) Tj T*
(consumption of bee products for a long period and frequent consumption of bee products per day ) Tj T*
(are associated with telomere length. An increase of year in consuming bee products is ) Tj T*
(associated with a mean increase in telomere length of 0.258 kbp. In addition, an increase in ) Tj T*
(frequency of eating bee products per day was also associated with a mean increase of 2.66 kbp ) Tj T*
(in telomere length. These results suggested that bee products might play some roles in ) Tj T*
(telomere length maintenance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
